  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale:\n   The central idea is to use a multi-stage optimization approach that combines global search with gradient-based refinement, but with an emphasis on diverse exploration and randomized restarts. Unlike the parent algorithm that uses DE and SLSQP, this approach introduces several key innovations:\n   - Multi-start differential evolution with diverse initial populations\n   - Strategic budget allocation across resolutions\n   - Temporal scaling of optimization intensity\n   These combine to avoid local optima and systematically explore the optimization landscape.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification:\n   The problem is to minimize:\n   \\[\\min_{h} C_5(h) = \\max_{k} \\left( \\int h(x) \\cdot (1 - h(x+k)) \\, dx \\right)\\]\n   Subject to:\n   \\[\\sum_{i=1}^{n} h_i \\Delta x = 1 \\quad \\& \\quad 0 \\leq h_i \\leq 1\\]\n   For discrete grid representation with dx\u00b2/n = 170, where \\Delta x=2/n.\n\n   Representation: h is represented as a vector h \u2208 [0,1]\u207f with sum h i = n/2.\n   Objective: Mode='full' correlation metric scaled by dx (2.0/n)\n\n3. Implementation Procedure:\n   Phase 1: Initialization\n     a. Generate diverse candidates by combining parent solution with random mutations\n     b. project_feasible function ensures sum constraint and bounds\n     c. time_points = [0, int(budget_s/5), int(budget_s/2), int(budget_s/32), int(budget_s/4)]\n\n   Phase 2: Global Optimization\n     a. DEParameter aggressive = {'maxiter': int(800 * n_points/170), 'polish': False}  (3 lines)\n     b. DE on n_div=12 parallel processes for budget_allocation\n        - Check feasibility first archiving best solution\n     c. Top-5%n \u2192 further refinement\n\n   Phase 3: Local Refinement\n     a. Apply targeted coordinate descent:\n        deltas = [\u00b10.01, \u00b10.005, \u00b10.001] relative to \u03c3(n)  (1 line)\n     b. Use projected gradient ascent until convergence\n     c. Budget for phase: 30% of total time\n\n   Phase 4: Resolution Handling\n     a. Dynamic resolution allocation:\n        if n < 170: use interpolation (Nearest neighbor mapping)\n        else if n > 170: use Fourier interpolation\n     b. Stochastic constraint check post-resampling\n     c. Time monitoring via sliding window\n\n4. Search Parameters:\n   - Mutation factor for DE: 0.85 amplified in early stages\n   - Gradient step size: 0.0025 * (1/old_score\u00b2)  (2 lines)\n   - Budget per resolution: 200s * (n/100)\n\n5. Budget and Robustness:\n   Estimation: Solve for t_max when sum_{\u03c1} budget_\u03c1 \u2264 1300\n   Real-time stopping: Monitor progress_ratio = |best_score - initial_score| / iterations\n\n6. Validation and Output:\n   - Re-evaluate final solution with mode='full' + manual checking\n   - Measure boundary enforcement variation\n   - Maintain solution validity_h: All samples \u2208 [0,1], sum\u2248n/2\n   - Compare using dx-normalized C5 metric\n\nDetailed Implementation Plan:\n\n1. Initialization:\n   h\u2080 = np.array(initial_h_values)\n   n_max = 340  (extensions)\n   projected_parent = project_feasible(h\u2080, n_max)\n\n2. Global Optimization State machine:\n   phase = 0\n   time_limits = [int(0.2*budget_s), int(0.4*budget_s), int(0.7*budget_s)]\n   candidate_pool = InitialPopulation(modes=['wrap', 'clip'], diversity_ratio=0.9)\n\n3. Main Loop:\n   while clock < budget_s:\n      if phase\u22610 (Global): \n          DE runs parallel=4 \n          top_x = sorted(np.unique([best,hits\u22648]), key=C5)[:5]\n          phase++ clock += time_limits[0]\n\n      elif phase\u22611 (Refinement):\n          for x in top_x: \n              optimize via projected LBFGS for 800 steps\n          phase++ clock += time_limits[1]\n\n      elif phase\u22612 (Resolution):\n          if n < n_max/2: upscale by upsample()\n          else: stability = Check_arithmetic_filters()\n          phase++ clock += time_limits[2]\n\n4. Local Search Strategy:\n   tend = warmest_optimization_stage\n   Do:\n      x_new = x_old + (np.random.randn(len(h)) * tend * adaptive)\n      project x_new\n   Until satisfies constraints to tolerance 1e-4\n\n5. Evaluation Protocol:\n   - Main C5 via mode='full' correlation\n   - Alternative measure: mode='valid' then extrapolate\n   - Lower is better; track best_score_noload.avg_coercion\n\n6. Termination Conditions:\n   if no_improvement(last=100) or time_close(budget_s):\n      log(\"Stuck: %s\" % str(best_score))\n      return best_solution, best_c5, n\n\nInnovations:\n- Temporal budget shaping by recycle factor (1.2 daily) to prolong exploration\n- Progressive trust region relaxation: start_delta=0.03, expand linearly until 0.6 variance\n- Context-sensitive repair (for C5 instability)\n- Directed mutation based on current optimum structure\n\nLet's implement this structured optimization with:\n   n_cand_init = 20\n   while time_avail(budget_s) and nottimers.done:\n      candidates = DE(f=smooth_max_val+margin, trail=last5)\n      new_cand = clipproject(candidates+GaussNoise)\n      accept_rate = analyzepromising(candidates)\n      if accept_rate>p_threshold:\n          budget_callback(failed=False)\n      else:\n          budget_callback(case='Penalty')\n\nAll helper functions should:\n   - Validate inputs\n   - Check feasibility via temporary projection\n   - Communicate ready_state ('_init', '_iter', '_final')\n   - Maintain resolution affinity\n\nLet's now benchmark structure against fake data...",
